[TITLE:e200 Cores Validation Results - Manual vs Implementation]

[INTRO]
This document tracks the validation of LLVM e200 core implementation against
official reference manuals. Results are documented here as validation progresses.

MANUAL_REFERENCES:
- e200z0: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z0.pdf (E200Z0CRM, Rev. 0, 4/2008)
- e200z4: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z4.pdf (e200z4RM, Rev. 0, 10/2009)

VALIDATION_STATUS:
- Started: Manual extraction and comparison in progress
- Priority: Instruction timing (CERT-001) and interrupt handling (CERT-003)

[VALIDATION-CERT-001-PIPELINE]
UID: VAL-CERT-001
TITLE: e200z0 Pipeline Architecture Validation

MANUAL_CHAPTER: Chapter 4 - Instruction Pipeline and Execution Timing

PIPELINE_STAGES_VERIFICATION:
Status: VALIDATED
Manual_States: 4-stage pipeline (IF, ID, EX, WB)
LLVM_Implementation: ✓ Correctly models 4 stages
Code_Location: PPCScheduleE200Z0.td:19-28
Notes: Manual confirms no separate MEM stage - memory operations in EX stage.
Our fix (CERT-002) was correct.

FUNCTIONAL_UNITS_VERIFICATION:
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Manual_Should_List:
- ALU (Integer ALU)
- BU (Branch Unit)  
- LSU (Load/Store Unit)
- MUL (Multiply Unit)
LLVM_Implementation: ✓ All units defined (lines 32-35)
Code_Location: PPCScheduleE200Z0.td:32-35
Next_Step: Verify resource sharing constraints from manual

INSTRUCTION_LATENCIES_VERIFICATION:
Status: PENDING_EXTRACTION
Required_From_Manual:
- Chapter 4, Section 4.X: Instruction timing tables
- Verify each instruction class latency:
  * Integer simple: 1 cycle (modeled as 1)
  * Integer compare: 1-2 cycles (modeled as 1 or 2)
  * Multiply: 4 cycles (modeled as 4)
  * Divide: 34 cycles (modeled as 34)
  * Load: 3 cycles (modeled as 3 in itinerary)
  * Store: 3 cycles (modeled as 3)
  * Branch: 1 cycle (modeled as 1)
  * SPR ops: 1 cycle (modeled as 1)

BYPASS_PATHS_VERIFICATION:
Status: PENDING_EXTRACTION
Manual_Should_Describe:
- GPR bypass (register forwarding)
- CR bypass (condition register forwarding)
LLVM_Implementation: ✓ Both defined (lines 41-42)
Code_Location: PPCScheduleE200Z0.td:41-42
Next_Step: Verify forwarding latency from manual

BRANCH_MISPREDICTION_VERIFICATION:
Status: PENDING_EXTRACTION
Current_Model: 3 cycles
Manual_Location: Chapter 4 - Branch prediction/timing
Next_Step: Extract exact penalty from manual

LOAD_TO_USE_LATENCY_VERIFICATION:
Status: PENDING_EXTRACTION
Current_Model: 4 cycles (3 pipeline + 1 writeback)
Manual_Location: Chapter 4 - Load/store timing
Next_Step: Verify against manual specification

[VALIDATION-CERT-003-INTERRUPTS]
UID: VAL-CERT-003
TITLE: Interrupt Handler Context Save Validation

MANUAL_CHAPTER: Chapter 5 - Interrupts and Exceptions

RFI_INSTRUCTION_VERIFICATION:
Status: PENDING_EXTRACTION
Manual_Location: Chapter 5 - Returning from exception handler (RFI)
LLVM_Implementation: ✓ Uses RFI for interrupt returns (line 1683)
Code_Location: PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1662-1686
Current_Behavior: Checks for VLE, uses E_RFI if VLE enabled
Next_Step: Verify RFI/e_rfi semantics from manual Section 5.27

INTERRUPT_CONTEXT_SAVE_VERIFICATION:
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Manual_Chapter: Chapter 5 - Exception handling, Chapter 2 - Register model

Register_Save_Requirements:
GPR_Save:
  Status: PARTIALLY_VALIDATED
  LLVM_Implementation: ✓ Saves GPRs based on usage tracking
  Code_Location: PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1855-1913
  Manual_Requirement: Extract from Chapter 5

CR_Save:
  Status: PARTIALLY_VALIDATED
  LLVM_Implementation: ✓ Saves CR if used
  Code_Location: PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1860-1893
  Manual_Requirement: Extract from Chapter 5

LR_Save:
  Status: PARTIALLY_VALIDATED
  LLVM_Implementation: ✓ Saves LR
  Code_Location: PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1856
  Manual_Requirement: Verify from manual

SPR_Save:
  Status: MISSING
  LLVM_Implementation: ✗ Not saved
  Code_Location: PPCFrameLowering.cpp:1843-1913
  Manual_Requirement: Extract which SPRs must be saved from Chapter 5

FPR_Save:
  Status: N/A_FOR_E200Z0
  Note: e200z0 has no FPU, so no FPR save needed

FPSCR_Save:
  Status: N/A_FOR_E200Z0
  Note: e200z0 has no FPU, so no FPSCR save needed

IVOR_TABLE_VERIFICATION:
Status: PENDING_EXTRACTION
